<title>INDIA: India abolishes 7.5 percent corporate surcharge.</title>
<headline>India abolishes 7.5 percent corporate surcharge.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>India on Friday proposed abolishing a 7.5 percent corporate surcharge and removing a tax on income from dividends.</p>
<p>Finance Minister P. Chidambaram also told parliament while presenting the 1997/98 (April-March) federal budget that the corporate tax on domestic firms would be cut to 35 percent from 40 percent and on foreign firms to 48 percent from 55 percent.</p>
</text>
